import sys
p = sys.argv[1]
lines = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| 676 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1
rows = [
"| 677 | 2026-10-26 | **Scales Further, the second Grades 2-3 room (Build AK).** Built on row 676. Board call 14, in her order. New chapter `scales-23` (chapter 31) on the Grades 2-3 floor after Hear and Sing Further; Technique door group kpl-23 after Playing scales; Stories of music moves to 32-34. Technique is comparable, not a copy (her 10:19): the room teaches the skills the Grade 2 and 3 scales add, and the keys and speeds sit in the teacher's copy. Every key, speed and fingering was read off the technical work book (Grade 2 pp36-39, Grade 3 pp47-50, transcribed 26 Oct; pp37, 47, 48 checked by eye): two octaves, mf, clear even legato, two notes a beat at crotchet 84 (Grade 2) and 92 (Grade 3), contrary motion 66 and 80; G melodic minor hands separately (Grade 2), C melodic minor hands together too (Grade 3); chromatic from D (Grade 2, hands separately), from A and D#/Eb (Grade 3, hands separately and together). Steps: (1) Start on a black key: her rule (2026-09-19) that the right hand starts on 2 and the thumb takes the first white key; tap the thumb's keys (ScfThumbPad, SCF fingerings for D, B minor, Bb, G minor, A, F# minor, Eb, C minor). (2) Where the thumbs meet, two octaves hands together (ScfStrip, ScfMeetPad): only on the middle keynote in D, A, G minor and C minor; on B and E in B minor; never in Bb, Eb and F# minor. (3) The melodic minor (ScfMelPad): up with the 6th and 7th raised, down natural. (4) Mirror twins, or not? (ScfMirrorPad, SCF_CM): contrary motion from one note, each hand with its own fingering; G, E minor, D minor, D, G minor mirror; F, B minor, Bb don't. (5) Chromatic from any note (ScfChromPad, chromFinger): 3 on black, 1 on white, 2 on the right hand's F and C and the left hand's E and B. Drill levels thumb, meet, mel, mirror, chrom; Home scf-thumb, scf-meet, scf-mel, scf-mirror, scf-chrom (HOME_FLOOR '23'); Lesson Book of 7 pages (scfLbPages); teacher's copy ScfTeacher with every fingering, key and speed. No Workbook yet (next). Also fixed: SCALES.Bb and SCALES.Eb two-octave left hand top note 3 -> 2, as the book prints it (Grade 2 p37, Grade 3 p48). Tests ak704.js, ak704b.js, chsweep (35 chapters), booksweep, reg674. |",
]
for r in reversed(rows): lines.insert(idx[0] + 1, r)
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(lines)); print('ok')
